Error [E0743]: Dynamic call `Shape::area` has no effect bound
  --> tests/ui/effect_trait_dispatch_unbounded.jet:5:39
    |
  5 | fn clean(shape: Shape) Int -[]> shape.area()
    |                                       ^^^^
 Why: A trait value can select any implementation at runtime, so an enclosing effect ceiling needs the trait method's declared upper bound
 Fix: Declare an effect row on `Shape::area`, such as `-[]>` for pure dispatch, or move this dynamic call outside the bounded function
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0743
